<description>&lt;p&gt;President De la Espriella faces rising armed violence as a police academy attack killed 21 people and protests over tax plans and spending cuts sweep the country. He ordered a tenth bombing against a narcoterrorist target in Valle del Cauca and called on the United States to prosecute former President Petro. U.S. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth arrived in Bogotá, delivered a C-130, met De la Espriella and announced a US-Venezuela military partnership, while Colombia rejected a U.S. proposal for joint anti-drug strikes. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxPLUdEX2NMaFBqSWQ4RlNLd2hUcEJrQmEyODV4TXlnTk1IR3hUeUxfRnZ5UDJOVFNZX1llSjRiT1RYTXNhc2tycjhMUUh2ejBscXIzMXVlOU44a21oWVlDb1AyU2RLNG12d0pGLUZpaW5PTlVEWkJEckxGVDYtOUtLWG4yeUk1VHgwTkVYNGdYenVrZXBhZjF4UURyaWExU2JYaDk5dU5XaGpHTEh1XzNWOVI5YnEtUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPX3pBcEVuWWJFX0FsRUI1eElBWUFETDBTT09PdTJkTldsRjRzU3ZFcXE0UTd5RXRJdmVLRVc4MEh2S3ZpSUpJbXlETjZyZ3V3X3RZMHhoN1ZaQS0yNTY1dk1qTDNLbjhtOEdnNWtuYjMteFIxOGNEZlRSOE02TnV4RWUxejdTVmxXU0ZKQTY0VEpDSDg?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxOUG1qb1J6eDE3OGIyZi1IWFBkMHFlVEZNR3M4ZFNnaS1tcHZnTGo2WU9ZM3F3bklQaDNBQlpqb1ZGUDNzUFFnUGI0V09PcldkTUd2MGItZ0FLbm5MbElrOFNndzJfX1BjekgxdWNqRy0zQ1Y2QzEtN0ZBVU5FaEpPclAtY2NoRGZrTC02U3doWEJneTVjbHZ6dHE2elk0ZkRycTZTbzdxYzRoOWJ5X2wyeA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latinoamérica 21&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMibEFVX3lxTE5yWVB0bHpQcW53Z29BQmVfNHZZZmN3dGRrZ1BMY3lhX21VVTVvemNwZ3NaZXYzbjFSanhkZ2tFc1NuZDZYQnFoX2xOOFFLdmY4NkVLNWswalpoZUhqV